<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khanate of Bukhara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1501">1501</a>–<a href="/years/1785">1785</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Khanate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a> was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbeks">Uzbek</a> monarchy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> from 1501 to 1785, founded by the Shaybanid dynasty, a branch of the Abu'l-Khayrids. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-shaybani">Muhammad Shaybani</a>, grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abul-khayr-khan">Abu'l-Khayr Khan</a>, conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkh">Balkh</a>, Bukhara, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tashkent">Tashkent</a>, but Shah <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismail-i">Ismail I</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a> killed him outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merv">Merv</a> in 1510. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdullah-khan-ii">Abdullah Khan II</a> made Bukhara the permanent capital by 1562, and in the 17th and 18th centuries the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janid-dynasty">Janid dynasty</a>, the last Chinggisid dynasty to rule Bukhara, held the throne. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> conquered the khanate in 1740; in 1785 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-murad">Shah Murad</a> formalised the rule of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manghit-dynasty">Manghit dynasty</a>, and it became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of Bukhara.</p></div>
